Ed,

thanks!

You were right - I was specifying my own priors and forgot to adjust them to JAGS (since I normally use the default stan option).

The models involved a comparison among the two SEM models below, which will be attached to a hierarchical MPT model.

Now, one issue I still have not been able to resolve is that jags.parallel() does not accept the initial values in jagtrans$inits - also even when I try to collect them as list of lists in the following manner (to avoid the "c1":"c4" labels):

inits <- list(list(parvec = jagtrans$inits$c1$parvec),
              list(parvec = jagtrans$inits$c2$parvec),
              list(parvec = jagtrans$inits$c3$parvec),
              list(parvec = jagtrans$inits$c4$parvec))

I continue getting a strange error massage that "length(inits) != n.chains", also even when I explicitly set "n.chain = length(inits)" in the function call!

As a work-around, I am now fitting the models in runjags(), but I have some custom functions that are tailored to jags.parallel(), so would still grateful for a solution for how to supply the initial values to that function.

#SEM models

mediation_model_latent_1a <- '
#measurement model
C =~ C1 + C2 + C3 + C4
N =~ Npre + Npro

#Regressions
C ~ gc*G + pc*P + tc*T
P ~ gp*G
T ~ pt*P
N ~ gn*G+pn*P + tn*T
I ~ gi*G+pi*P + ti*T

C ~~ N
C ~~ I
N ~~ I
C1 ~~ C2 + C3 + C4
C2 ~~ C3 + C4
C3 ~~ C4
Npre ~~ Npro

C1~~C1
C2~~C2
C3~~C3
C4~~C4
Npre~~Npre
Npro~~Npro
P~~P
T~~T
N~~N
I~~I
G~~G

# indirect effect (a*b)
indirect_N := gp*pn
indirect_I := gp*pi
indirect_C := gp*pc
# total effect
total_N := gn + (gp*pn)
total_I := gi + (gp*pi)
total_C := gc + (gp*pc)
prop.mediated_N := indirect_N / total_N
prop.mediated_I := indirect_I / total_I
prop.mediated_C := indirect_C / total_C
'

mediation_model_latent_2a <- '
#measurement model
C =~ C1 + C2 + C3 + C4
N =~ Npre + Npro

#Regressions
C ~ pc*P + tc*T
P ~ gp*G
T ~ pt*P
N ~ pn*P + tn*T
I ~ pi*P + ti*T

C ~~ N
C ~~ I
N ~~ I
C1 ~~ C2 + C3 + C4
C2 ~~ C3 + C4
C3 ~~ C4
Npre ~~ Npro

C1~~C1
C2~~C2
C3~~C3
C4~~C4
Npre~~Npre
Npro~~Npro
P~~P
T~~T
N~~N
I~~I
G~~G
'

Thanks!
Niels

