Niels,

I looked at the R2jags package a bit to try to figure it out. The inits seem to work as expected if you use jags() instead of jags.parallel(). For example, this command worked:

jags(data = jagtrans$data, inits = jagtrans$inits, parameters.to.save = "parvec", model.file = 'lavExport/sem.jag')

I then got the same error as you with jags.parallel(). I think it is because each chain is sent to a separate core, via a call to jags(). And it does the n.chains vs length(inits) comparison after the chains are sent to each core, so it sees n.chains=1 and length(inits)=4. I think this means that, currently, you can only send one set of inits that is used by all chains:

jags.parallel(data = jagtrans$data, inits = jagtrans$inits[1], parameters.to.save = "parvec", model.file = 'lavExport/sem.jag')

I guess that this is not the desired behavior, and you might contact the R2jags maintainer to fix it.

Ed

